# Keep LF line endings in the working tree on every platform, also on Windows
# checkouts with core.autocrlf=true.
#
# The shell scripts, the SLURM scripts and the Allrun template are executed on
# Linux (natively, in a container or on a cluster), often after being copied
# from a Windows checkout; a carriage return in them breaks bash. Python, YAML
# and Markdown files are kept LF as well, so that copied files and their hashes
# do not depend on the platform of the checkout.
#
# cfd/solvers/scalarTransportFoamTurbulent/ has its own .gitattributes
# (everything LF, for wmake).
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.slurm   text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
cfd/templates/Allrun  text eol=lf
*.cff     text eol=lf
*.txt     text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
